        setup: {
          players: 'One player only. Algerian is a solitaire (patience) game played by a single player.',
          deck: 'Two standard 52-card decks shuffled together (104 cards).',
          equipment: 'Standard tabletop or digital interface.',
          dealing: '1. **Foundations**: 8 slots (initially empty or 4 Aces/4 Kings placed if drawn). 2. **Tableau**: 8 depots with 1 card each. 3. **Reserve**: 6 piles with 4 cards each. 4. **Stock**: Remainder of the 104 cards.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Consolidate all 104 cards into the 8 foundation piles (A-K and K-A).',
          gameplay: '1. Deal layout: 8 tableau depots (1 card each), 6 reserve piles (4 cards each), stock = remainder. 2. Play phase: Move exposed top cards from reserve or tableau to foundations (4 A-up, 4 K-down in suit) or build on tableau in ascending/descending suit (wrap King-Ace). Vacant depots accept any exposed card. Reserve piles cannot be built on. 3. Redeal: When no moves, deal 2 more cards to each reserve; repeat until 8 cards left, then 1 per depot. 4. Win when all 104 cards are on foundations.',
          keyRules: [
            'The reserve piles cannot be built upon; they only serve as sources of cards.',
            'Empty tableau depots can be filled by ANY available card.',
            'The game is won only when ALL cards are on foundations.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prioritize emptying the reserve piles. Since you cannot build on them, they act as bottlenecks that hide 24 cards at the start.',
          intermediate: "Manage your foundations evenly. If you build one suit too far up, you might find that the corresponding descending foundation for that suit is blocked by cards you've already 'packed away'.",
          advanced: "Utilization of the 'Meeting Point': Strategic transfers between the ascending and descending foundations can be used to free up a specific card needed for the tableau.",
          tips: [
            "Avoid filling empty tableau spaces immediately. Keep them as 'temporary parking' for cards that are blocking deep reserve piles.",
            "Because you can build both up and down, try to keep 'middle' cards (7, 8, 9) on the tableau where they have the most building options.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
